<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Korea Flour buys 16,900T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Korea Flour buys 16,900T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Flour Milling Corp said on Tuesday it bought 16,900 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Kanematsu Corp.</p>
<p>The company passed on tenders for another 16,900 tonnes with shipment for September 1-30 due to higher-than-expected prices, an official with Korea Flour said.  </p>
<p>The official said arrival was set to the western port city of Mokpo. Shipment was slated for August 5-September 5 from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>Details for the purchase are as follows:</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	     Tonne	Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  5,100	 $140.35</p>
<p>(protein min 10.0%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  2,600	 $139.25</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	   4,400	 $146.35</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring    4,800	 $170.95</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
